        "headingId": 1088,
        "headingText": "<font color=\"red\">Classification in progress, Data not available in this Beta</font>",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:54:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1073,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 1089,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152065,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 89,
        "headingId": 1089,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> female adnexal tumour of probable Wolffian origin.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:54:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1074,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 1090,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152066,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 89,
        "headingId": 1090,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:54:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1075,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 1091,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152067,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 89,
        "headingId": 1091,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most arise in the broad ligament {4693596; 10414506; 31591497; 38919071}, with rare tumours developing in the ovary {6859387}, fallopian tube {30134342}, or non-adnexal sites {6624720; 8135182; 15512055; 30967956}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:54:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1076,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 1092,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152068,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 89,
        "headingId": 1092,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients range in age from 19&nbsp;to 83&nbsp;years (mean: 45&nbsp;years) and may present with abdominopelvic pain or abnormal bleeding; however, many cases are incidental findings {4693596; 10414506}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:54:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1077,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 1093,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152069,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 89,
        "headingId": 1093,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours are rare, with &lt;&nbsp;200&nbsp;cases reported in the English literature, mainly in middle-aged women {39949601}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:54:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1078,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 1094,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152070,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 89,
        "headingId": 1094,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:54:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1079,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 1095,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152071,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 89,
        "headingId": 1095,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>A Wolffian origin is favoured because these tumours arise along the path of the regressing Wolffian system.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:54:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1086,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 1102,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152072,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 89,
        "headingId": 1102,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours are often well circumscribed and solid or solid and cystic, ranging in size from&nbsp;8 to 300&nbsp;mm (mean: 60&ndash;100&nbsp;mm) {4693596; 10414506}. Haemorrhage, necrosis, or focal calcification may be seen.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:54:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1080,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 1096,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152073,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 89,
        "headingId": 1096,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours are composed of an admixture of hollow to solid tubules, sieve-like cysts, and diffuse growth {4693596; 10414506; 31591497; 38919071}. Hyalinized bands may be prominent (imparting a nodular appearance) or delicate and interspersed within the stroma. Cells are cuboidal to ovoid to occasionally spindled, with scant cytoplasm, small nuclei, and inconspicuous to small nucleoli. PAS-positive eosinophilic luminal secretions may be present; cytological atypia and mitoses are usually minimal.</p>\r\n<p>Tumours show variable expression of sex cord stromal, epithelial, and mesothelial markers, hormone receptors, and CD10; but they are usually negative for EMA, claudin-4, PAX8, GATA3, and TTF1 {10414506; 26135559; 26352548; 30134342; 38919071}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:54:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1081,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 1097,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152074,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 89,
        "headingId": 1097,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:54:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1082,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 1098,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152075,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 89,
        "headingId": 1098,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Wolffian tumours lack recurring genomic alterations {30134342; 31591497}. In challenging cases, molecular analysis may be helpful to exclude morphological mimickers including mesonephric/mesonephric-like carcinoma (<em>KRAS/NRAS)</em>, STK11 adnexal tumour<em> (STK11</em>), sex cord stromal tumours (<em>FOXL2, DICER1</em>), endometrioid carcinoma (<em>PTEN, PIK3CA, ARID1A</em>), and peritoneal mesothelioma (<em>BAP1, CDKN2A, NF2</em>).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:54:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1085,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 1101,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152076,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 89,
        "headingId": 1101,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> typically broad ligament origin; tubular, sieve-like, and/or solid growth.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:54:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1083,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 1099,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152077,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 89,
        "headingId": 1099,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not applicable</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:54:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1084,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 1100,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152078,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 89,
        "headingId": 1100,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Wolffian tumours are usually benign. Rare recurrences have been reported {6859387; 8135638; 38919071}, some of which were associated with incomplete excision {33787642} or iatrogenic dissemination {40062785}. Many tumours previously classified as malignant probably represent morphological mimickers {35395118}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:54:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]